  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Compute the sum of the first $6$ terms of the geometric series $-4+1-\\frac{1}{4}+\u22ef.$\n\nExpress your answer as a fraction (do not round your answer).\n\n${S}_{6}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Given a geometric series, the sum of the first $N$ terms is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}={a}_{1}\\frac{(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r},\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term of the series and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nIn our case, ${a}_{1}=-4.$ To find the value of $r,$ we find the ratio of the first two terms in the series:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{1}{-4}=-\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nIf we substitute ${a}_{1}=-4,\\,N=6,$ and $r=-\\frac{1}{4}$ into our formula, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{6} & =-4\\cdot \\frac{(1-{(-\\frac{1}{4})}^{6})}{(1-(-\\frac{1}{4}))} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{(1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{6})}{(1+\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{(\\frac{{4}^{6}-1}{{4}^{6}})}{(\\frac{5}{4})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{16}{5}\\cdot (\\frac{{4}^{6}-1}{{4}^{6}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{16}{5}\\cdot \\frac{4\\,095}{4\\,096} \\\\  & =-\\frac{819}{256}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
